  "query_preview": "(This evening through Tuesday)...\nIssued at 158 PM EST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon through Wednesday...\n\nWarm and breezy conditions will continue for the rest of the \nafternoon ahead of an approaching system. \n\nThis evening will be quiet for most areas. Overnight into Wednesday \nmorning, a good (around 50kt) 850mb jet will aid in transporting \nmoisture into the area. Forcing from an upper wave rotating around \nan upper low will work with this moisture to produce widespread rain \nacross central Indiana. \n\nThe wind field above the surface will be strong, but instability \nwill be quite weak. Not expecting any severe weather, but some gusty \nshowers or an isolated gusty storm will be possible.\n\nAfter the main area of rain exits Monday, there looks to be enough \nforcing and moisture for a narrow line of convection to develop \nalong a surface cold front as it moves through during the afternoon. \nInstability is quite poor, so not expecting any strong convection \nand likely not any thunder.\n\nRainfall amounts may reach around an inch in portions of the \nsoutheast, with less than a quarter of an inch expected northwest.\n\nLows tonight will only be in the lower 60s thanks to southerly flow \nahead of the cold front. With the cold front moving through on \nWednesday, highs will generally be in the upper 60s, with around 70 \npossible east if rain exits fast enough. Lows Wednesday night will \nbe in the 40s.\n\nThursday and Friday...\n\nThursday looks quiet ahead of an approaching upper trough and \nsurface cold front. The trough and cold front will move through \nThursday night into Friday. Moisture will be limited with the Gulf \ncut off. Will have some mainly slight chance PoPs on Friday, with \nthe most coverage expected during the first half of the day.\n\nHighs on Thursday will be in the lower to middle 60s, but Friday \nwill see mainly upper 50s for highs as cooler air moves in behind \nthe front.\n\nSaturday onward...\n\nNorthwest flow will continue Saturday into early next week. An upper \nlow moving through southeast Canada will bring another cold front on \nSunday. Similar to Friday though, moisture will be very limited with \nthe Gulf cut off again. Will go with a dry forecast through the \nentire period.\n\nThe cold front won't have much cold air behind it. Highs in the \nmiddle 50s on Saturday will gradually moderate to the lower and \nmiddle 60s by Tuesday. Lows will be near freezing for parts of the \narea Saturday and Sunday nights.",
